                    {
                        "form_id": "4951a791-c03a-4fa4-910e-2f63dd780e86",
                        "entry_id": "921c88a0-4918-3073-b14d-5015951b83c4",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "co-auteur"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2d65b81e-0300-3163-abd6-35b9870ea7ff",
                        "entry_id": "921c88a0-4918-3073-b14d-5015951b83c4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Auteur d’un ouvrage écrit en collaboration."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20ff22fb-5e94-4673-8818-1878b8512bd4",
                                "sense_id": "2d65b81e-0300-3163-abd6-35b9870ea7ff",
                                "text": "Elle sera accompagnée de son coauteur, l’illustrateur François Ravard."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de44c8f5-7de6-43f4-a405-7f5f817adf6c",
                                "sense_id": "2d65b81e-0300-3163-abd6-35b9870ea7ff",
                                "text": "« Dans cette saison 2, on essaie d’explorer la liberté de pensée des années 1980, associée à cette envie de capitalisme… Comment jongler avec des deux quêtes presque antinomiques ? », analyse Emmanuel Poulain-Arnaud, cocréateur et coauteur de la série."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a283af5-94d5-4236-9904-8d264b87e674",
                                "sense_id": "2d65b81e-0300-3163-abd6-35b9870ea7ff",
                                "text": "Si ces espèces benthiques (oursins, ophiures, petits crabes et crustacés…) avaient été fortement modifiées, nous aurions assisté à un changement des espèces de poissons débarquées, puisque la plupart s’en nourrissent, commente Joël Veigneau, chercheur à l’Ifremer et coauteur d’une étude initiée par les acteurs de la pêche de Normandie et des Hauts-de-France."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9645d649-5f05-3b0e-8def-fe2ed14482ee",
                        "entry_id": "921c88a0-4918-3073-b14d-5015951b83c4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Complice dans une action."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3718399a-4cbc-4e63-806d-e6bd731094ec",
                                "sense_id": "9645d649-5f05-3b0e-8def-fe2ed14482ee",
                                "text": "Vainement dirait-on avec M. Rauter, que les coauteurs sont auteurs par complicité et nécessairement complices les uns des autres, puisqu’ils s’aident réciproquement dans les faits qui consomment l’action."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80aa4d2c-0c97-4a86-9314-ff62933f4c47",
                        "source_entry_id": "921c88a0-4918-3073-b14d-5015951b83c4",
                        "source_sense_description": "auteur en collaboration",
                        "target_lang_word": "Koautor",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Koautor",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf04dc07-6613-3e5e-ae3b-75738673ec02",
                                        "entry_id": "04080bfb-7b01-32a2-9118-7a541e1242b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(männliche^☆) Person, die ein literarisches Werk zusammen mit einer anderen Person oder mehreren anderen Personen verfasst hat"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "501b7dc7-def2-41fd-9a8b-10eba195e58d",
                                                "sense_id": "bf04dc07-6613-3e5e-ae3b-75738673ec02",
                                                "text": "Dank der Recherche meines Koautors und besten Freundes gelang es uns, die historischen Gegebenheiten ziemlich exakt darzustellen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47f57101-9e42-4393-83f8-7edc83edceab",
                                                "sense_id": "bf04dc07-6613-3e5e-ae3b-75738673ec02",
                                                "text": "Ein „Hans Müller“ wird auf dem Umschlag des Romans als Koautor genannt."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9f1b4d3e-485a-450c-bf0f-7a7db7ac39d1",
                        "source_entry_id": "921c88a0-4918-3073-b14d-5015951b83c4",
                        "source_sense_description": "auteur en collaboration",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mitautor",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mitautor",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71c727d8-d9f8-382c-a7ff-557b9085ea30",
                                        "entry_id": "3fb7f867-1b40-392e-b27d-dee574b69b21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eine Person, die zugleich (auch/mit) als schreibende Person (Autor) tätig ist; eine von zwei oder mehreren Personen, die gemeinsam einen Text verfassen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16c70f02-2f2a-4ee8-b18b-bb315434b246",
                                                "sense_id": "71c727d8-d9f8-382c-a7ff-557b9085ea30",
                                                "text": "„Mein Vater wurde übrigens ohne sein Wissen Mitautor von ‚Göttliche Erkenntnis‘, er blieb deswegen auch, insbesondere mangels seiner Einwilligung und weil ich seinen Text komplett sprachlich bearbeitete, als Autor unerwähnt.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1998fb2f-7f26-440e-b5d0-8e48ff39ab74",
                        "source_entry_id": "921c88a0-4918-3073-b14d-5015951b83c4",
                        "source_sense_description": "auteur en collaboration",
                        "target_lang_word": "coauthor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "coauthor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e925004-c646-30dd-8c2e-ebb076dc5469",
                                        "entry_id": "69cbdd71-645d-30de-98a1-06bab0e1cd33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An author who collaborates with another to write something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f5abbc2-ec0b-40dd-8d9d-26fecf8140d2",
                                                "sense_id": "0e925004-c646-30dd-8c2e-ebb076dc5469",
                                                "text": "Following this trail, we treat our sample coauthor network as a causal graph and, using SDP relaxations, rule out latent homophily as a manifestation of prior shared interest leading to the observed patternedness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbfcf420-0475-4618-875c-2135e25b373a",
                                                "sense_id": "0e925004-c646-30dd-8c2e-ebb076dc5469",
                                                "text": "In a 2022 paper, Dr. Baumert and his coauthors pointed out that the algorithms companies use to determine these scores are often proprietary and not scientifically vetted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e90b2379-757e-4b44-b661-6a5487a7c3f3",
                                                "sense_id": "0e925004-c646-30dd-8c2e-ebb076dc5469",
                                                "text": "“There is strong evidence that 76 known or potential breast carcinogens from food contact materials recently purchased all over the world can be found in people,” said study coauthor Jane Muncke, managing director and chief scientific officer at the Food Packaging Forum, a nonprofit foundation based in Zurich, Switzerland, that focuses on science communication and research."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "coauthor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6659cf9a-e8e4-3a19-bc0b-a1b4de6f2fad",
                                        "entry_id": "2b97eaa5-c8dc-3c58-98db-886ddd3b3ae4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To write something in collaboration with another author."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cb40909-2696-4905-ad8c-de58fcefda9e",
                                                "sense_id": "6659cf9a-e8e4-3a19-bc0b-a1b4de6f2fad",
                                                "text": "My intent in writing this book, as was the case in coauthoring Unfit for Command, is to fully document all arguments and contentions I make, extensively footnoting all references, so readers can determine for themselves the truth and validity of the factual claims."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18ed3e2e-24e0-4ba9-89c2-68991d5bbd82",
                                                "sense_id": "6659cf9a-e8e4-3a19-bc0b-a1b4de6f2fad",
                                                "text": "Almost immediately after the video went semiviral, activist Rosa Clemente mobilized a group of women of color to coauthor and sign a statement denouncing the video, calling for XXL to feature anti–sexual violence content and demanding the firing of then–XXL editor-in-chief, Vanessa Satten.⁴²"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d75c1f2f-e6bb-450e-ae63-e1bb3d6902cc",
                                                "sense_id": "6659cf9a-e8e4-3a19-bc0b-a1b4de6f2fad",
                                                "text": "“It’s a positive outcome if you don’t have to live together after you’ve broken up,” said Natasha Pilkauskas, an associate professor at the University of Michigan who coauthored the study. “It allows people to live in the way they want to be living.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
